{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/y90nupkv","slide":1,"text":"Draft poster for Project 59. Students: Eddie Kim and Jeruh Kim. Supervisor: Ho Seok Ahn. Contact: hkim807@aucklanduni.ac.nz.\n\nSources: /Users/eddiekim/Downloads/Poster Design Guide.pdf (A1 portrait, required fields, PDF <50 MB). Its 2024 deadline is historical. /Users/eddiekim/Downloads/Speech_Nilushika2023.pdf. Layout reference: /Users/eddiekim/Downloads/Poster_77 (1).pdf.\n\nSurvey source: /Users/eddiekim/Downloads/Human Evaluation of Robot Behaviour (Responses).xlsx, Form responses 1. Preference counts and all 36 rating means independently verified against config/human-reference.json. Every preference bar sums to 37. Unable to judge is a survey response, not an action.\n\nPipeline source: docs/results/first-action-live-output/results.csv, report.md, verification.json. Nine SDK captures, first valid policy output, identical initial eligible states. qwen2.5:7b, temperature 0, seed 42, warmed model. Times are from replay start, not inference latency. All actions NOT_EXECUTED_OFFLINE.\n\nBoth policies produce outputs in S2,S3,S9. Six no-action cases remain in coverage denominator. LLM outputs fail live-client acceptance (S2 stale observation, S3 gaze not ready, S9 person no longer visible). Acceptance/timings reflect one development replay and may vary.\n\nThe survey clips are trimmed and trim offsets are unavailable. This prevents survey-end human-alignment scoring. Initial survey is completed. Human evaluation of actual completed-system behaviour is future work. Do not claim VLM/hybrid results or policy superiority.\n\nNavel product image: https://navelrobotics.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Navel0157-scaled.jpg via https://navelrobotics.com/en/navel-the-new-empathy-robot-for-good-care/. University logo extracted unchanged from supplied exemplar. Official department logo is a labelled draft field. No sponsor confirmed.\n\nFonts Rubik and Noto Sans are design selections evoking the robot, not verified official brand fonts.\n\nEvaluation sources: var/evaluation/poster-20261011-final-first-output-01/graph_data/scenario_comparison.csv and first_output_coverage.csv; output/poster/Evaluation_Findings_and_Poster_Plan_2026-10-11.md. Numbers describe the final scenario preset, first validated policy output, three paired replays, and offline SingleTrial client acceptance. First-output elapsed time includes evidence accumulation. Survey responses concern video endings and were not scored against these outputs. No physical execution.\n"}